From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: 1ma <hello@1ma.ai>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 12:07:07 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] 1ma: ~/.1ma data directory and telemetry off by default

1ma keeps its server data in ~/.1ma so it can sit next to an existing bb
install without sharing a database, and it sends no usage telemetry unless
the user sets BB_TELEMETRY=true. The places that name the default data
directory directly follow it: a server move archives and checks ~/.1ma,
never bb's ~/.bb; machine enrollment guards ~/.1ma; the Pi provider keeps
its bridge sessions in ~/.1ma. Tests follow the new defaults.
